  "about": "Haystack padding for the per-turn memory bench (haystack-bench.ts). recall-cases.json gives each caller 12-18 memories; this pads the store to hundreds with synthetic distractors so a fixed cosine floor is tested where it will live. near: same people, pets and places as the caller's real memories, factually different (a different ailment, city, day or teacher); never labelled as about a turn. generic: everyday memories on topics no labelled turn mentions, with {name} filled in. updates: an older fact and the newer one that supersedes it; a turn about it expects the newer one, so sending the older one is a wrong memory. backchannels: turns where the right answer is to send nothing. Every value here is invented.",
